---
import { BUSINESS } from '../config.ts';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="SolLock stores nothing about you: no accounts, no database, no analytics. Here is exactly what happens to your data.">
  <h1 class="section-title">Privacy</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>
      We store nothing about you. No accounts, no database, no analytics, no tracking cookies. What your browser asks the Solana
      network passes through our server without being logged.
    </p>

    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>
      {BUSINESS.tradeName}, {BUSINESS.place}{BUSINESS.kvk && `, KvK ${BUSINESS.kvk}`}. Contact: <a href={`mailto:${BUSINESS.email}`}>{BUSINESS.email}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What happens when you use SolLock</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Hosting.</strong> Cloudflare serves this website. Like any web server, it receives your IP address and browser details
        in order to deliver the pages and protect the site from attacks. We have switched off logging for our own server code. Cloudflare
        processes this data for us under its data processing agreement.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Rate limits.</strong> To stop abuse, Cloudflare counts how many requests come from your IP address each minute, in
        memory. The counts are not stored by us.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Blockchain requests.</strong> To build a lock and to find your locks, your browser asks the Solana network questions
        through our server, for example the balance of a wallet address. Those questions contain public addresses. Our server passes them
        on to our network providers, Helius and, as a backup, Alchemy, without your IP address or browser details, and does not log them.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Prices.</strong> Our server fetches today's Solana price from CoinGecko. CoinGecko never sees you or your request.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Nothing from other sites.</strong> Fonts and code come from our own domain. There are no third-party scripts, ads or
        trackers.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Your browser.</strong> Your browser remembers your theme, your currency and the wallet you connected last (in local
        storage), so you don't have to choose again. On an Android phone it also keeps the token your wallet app hands out when you
        connect, so the app recognises this site next time; that token goes only back to the same app. None of this reaches us, and
        none of it is used to track you. You can clear it in your browser settings.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Your wallet.</strong> Your wallet app is not ours. It has its own privacy policy.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>The blockchain is public</h2>
    <p>
      A lock is a transaction on Solana. It is public and permanent: anyone can see your wallet address, the amount, the unlock date
      and, for a gift, the recipient's address. Nobody can delete it, including us. A gift links the recipient's address to yours, so
      think about that before you lock a gift.
    </p>

    <h2>Why we may process this</h2>
    <p>
      Delivering the website and keeping it safe is our legitimate interest. Passing on the blockchain requests you make is needed to
      provide the service you ask for.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You have the right to access, correct and delete your personal data, and to object to its use. Because we store nothing about
      you, there is usually nothing for us to show or delete, but you can always ask. If you are unhappy with how we handle your data,
      you can complain to the Dutch Data Protection Authority, the Autoriteit Persoonsgegevens.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If this statement changes, the new version appears on this page. This version is dated 5 November 2026.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
